        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Railways: New York, Westchester and Boston Railway\n- Stations: Quaker Ridge\n- Places: South Bronx, Harlem River, Mount Vernon, White Plains, Port Chester, New Rochelle, Westchester County, New York\n\nFacts:\n- The New York, Westchester and Boston Railway ran from the southernmost part of the South Bronx near the Harlem River to Mount Vernon.\n- The New York, Westchester and Boston Railway had branches north to White Plains and east to Port Chester.\n- Mount Vernon is a city in Westchester County, New York, United States.\n- Quaker Ridge is a former railroad station on the White Plains branch of the New York, Westchester and Boston Railway in the city of New Rochelle in Westchester County, New York.",
